# Chronos browser tasks

- Each ChatGPT, Gemini, and DeepSeek task opens a new chat tab. Do not type a later task into an earlier conversation.
- Close that task tab after the reply and any generated media are stored. Leave the signed-in anchor tab open.
- If the new tab is already a human-verification page, do not navigate it again and do not inject script into it.
- ChatGPT and Gemini image tasks must return the image file with the reply. A caption by itself is not a finished image result.
- Judge image intent from the text after `User request:`, so saved instructions do not hide or force image capture.
- DeepSeek does not generate images. Do not add an image path for it.
- Task API responses omit saved and per-task instructions. Settings endpoints are the only place that returns saved instruction text.
